How this fits your diagram
User
  ↓
Voiceflow / Frontend
  ↓
API Gateway
  ↓
AWS Lambda
  │
  ├── Generate Embedding
  │
  ├── Search Qdrant
  │
  ├── Retrieve Documents
  │
  └── Call LLM
          ↓
     Generated Answer
          ↓
       Lambda
          ↓
    API Gateway
          ↓
Voiceflow / Frontend

The key part is that lambda_handler() is the entry point. AWS Lambda invokes this function when API Gateway sends a request.

If your project uses Groq instead of OpenAI, the LLM portion should be changed to Groq's API, while the overall Lambda architecture stays the same.

